{
 "schema": 1,
 "about": "Exploded and opened-base offsets (metres, robot frame: x forward, y left, z up), build-stage membership, short labels, view settings and the guided-tour keyframes for docs/assets/roadmap/exploded.html, keyed by the component ids of model/model.js and their GLB node or part ids. offsets: Explode robot; open: Open the base. Offsets move whole parts; no geometry changes. Checked by scripts/check_roadmap.py.",
 "stages_note": "Subsystem grouping for orientation. Not an assembly instruction; the 2.0 assembly guide is in preparation.",
 "stages": [
  {
   "n": 1,
   "title": "Chassis structure",
   "text": "Steel deck, front, rear and side panels, four corner supports and the centre bracket of CAD v0.2, the base design shared with release 001.",
   "frame": "base"
  },
  {
   "n": 2,
   "title": "Drive and castors",
   "text": "Two hub motor wheels with brakes (brake side inboard) on the drive axle and four swivel castors under the deck corners. The motor driver sits on its mount on the deck.",
   "frame": "base"
  },
  {
   "n": 3,
   "title": "Power and safety",
   "text": "Power and safety in the rear section (owner correction A1, 2 Nov 2026): the TZBOT WCM-500-24 receiver prepared at the rear panel on the centre line (installed later) with its 20 mm metal-free margin and the base-sheet cut-out, 4 + 4 EVE LF105 cells upright in two removable side pocket trays joined by the keyed connector PWR-018 on the series link across the centre (A9), and the power electronics on the MEC-006 plate above the receiver. The base E-stop (robot left) and the RESET button (robot right) on the front panel.",
   "frame": "base"
  },
  {
   "n": 4,
   "title": "Compute and base controller",
   "text": "Front electronics bay, one layout (owner correction A2, 2 Nov 2026): the MEC-005 plate on the base sheet with a second tier, the Jetson Orin NX 8 GB on its Robotics 104 carrier (D-01), the NUCLEO-H723ZG, the CAN and I/O modules, the converters, FB-C and the PNOZ s3 on a DIN carrier; the IMU board stays on the electronics bracket at imu_link.",
   "frame": "base"
  },
  {
   "n": 5,
   "title": "Near-field sensors, LiDAR and base camera",
   "text": "Four ultrasonic sensors and two ToF cliff sensors in the panel holes with their mounts, the 2D LiDAR on its support and spacer, and the base RGB-D camera behind the front slot.",
   "frame": "base"
  },
  {
   "n": 6,
   "title": "Cover",
   "text": "The top cover and its two sloped flanges close the base.",
   "frame": "base"
  },
  {
   "n": 7,
   "title": "Lift column and adapter plate",
   "text": "The lift base plate on the centre-frame arch, the DOLD Hexalift V4 column (drawn as a primitive; supplier CAD pending) and the one-piece 10 mm adapter plate on the column top (425 x 100 mm with a 65 mm rear extension, A6) with the second E-stop on it behind the post, button up (owner correction A5, 2 Nov 2026). On the rear face of the static profile: the three lift stop sensors; the flag rod hangs from the plate extension (A6).",
   "frame": [
    "lift_base_plate",
    "lift_column",
    "adapter_plate",
    "second_estop",
    "lift_stop_sensors",
    "flag_rod"
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 8,
   "title": "Arm profile and arms",
   "text": "The HFS6-60120 arm profile on the adapter plate, the two OpenArm 2.0 arms on their mounts and the head camera on its bracket (lens 57 mm ahead of the shoulder, 30 degrees down; A4). On the front of the profile, bottom up: the head light and the Getac ZX80 tablet in portrait (A3), the light top edge 10 mm below the Getac.",
   "frame": [
    "arm_profile",
    "openarm",
    "head_camera_bracket",
    "head_camera"
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 9,
   "title": "Harness",
   "text": "Every cable of the harness on its routed path, coloured by domain, with the P-clips, grommets, CAN terminations, the lift energy chain and the drawn fasteners. Proposed by the roadmap model; cable_list.csv gives each route.",
   "frame": "base"
  }
 ],
